  "reason": "Evidence: RNA (pca_n2000, singleprofile) achieves 48.5% acc while image (resnet50, singleprofile) is weak at 20.8%, establishing RNA as the dominant modality. Uncertainty: We have no evidence on whether the profile/aggregation axis (single vs. multiprofile with pooling) improves performance. This experiment (config_002: rna_only, multiprofile, pca_n2000, avgpool) directly compares to config_001 by changing only the profile setting and adding avgpool aggregation, isolating the effect of multi-profile representation with a simple, interpretable aggregator. It is the best next step because (1) it keeps the encoder fixed (pca_n2000) for a clean single-axis comparison, (2) the multiprofile+aggregation decision is a structural prerequisite that gates all downstream multimodal multiprofile experiments (configs 018–021, 030–033, etc.), so resolving it early maximizes information value for the remaining budget, and (3) avgpool is the simplest aggregation, giving a conservative baseline before testing transformer aggregation."
